\ The Jupiter Ace simulation: floating point. A number takes two cells,
\ four bytes: six BCD digits of mantissa and a byte holding the sign (bit
\ 7) and the exponent (bits 0-6, biased by 0x40), the value being
\ 0.d1d2d3d4d5d6 times ten to the exponent. 123.456 is the cells 0x3456
\ (below) and 0x4312 (on top); zero is four zero bytes. Loaded after
\ buffer.telic.

\ the six digits of a mantissa, first digit first, from the two cells
: mantissa-digits ( low high -- digits )
	| low high |
	[ high 255 bit-and low 8 rshift low 255 bit-and ] to digit-pairs
	[ ] to digits
	0 3 1 do k
		digit-pairs k @i to pair
		digits pair 4 rshift add-last! pair 15 bit-and add-last! drop
	loop
	digits ;

\ a float's value as a telic number
: float-value ( low high -- value )
	| low high |
	low high mantissa-digits 0 ( swap 10 * + ) reduce to mantissa
	mantissa 0 = if 0 exit then
	high 8 rshift to exponent-byte
	mantissa 1000000 / 10 exponent-byte 127 bit-and 64 - ^ * to value
	exponent-byte 128 bit-and if value negate else value then ;

\ the cells of a float from a sign, six digits and a decimal exponent, the value 0.digits times ten to it; ERROR 8 out of range, zero below it
: pack-float ( negative mantissa exponent -- low high )
	| negative mantissa exponent |
	mantissa 0 = if 0 0 exit then
	exponent 64 + to exponent-byte
	exponent-byte 1 < if 0 0 exit then
	exponent-byte 127 > if 8 ace-error then
	[ ] to digits
	mantissa to remaining
	0 6 1 do k
		digits remaining 10 mod add-last! drop
		remaining 10 / truncate to remaining
	loop
	digits reverse to digits
	digits 4 @i 16 * digits 5 @i + digits 2 @i 16 * digits 3 @i + 256 * + to low
	negative if 128 else 0 then exponent-byte bit-or to sign-and-exponent
	digits 0 @i 16 * digits 1 @i + sign-and-exponent 256 * + to high
	low high ;

\ a telic number as a float, rounded to six significant digits
: float-cells ( value -- low high )
	| value |
	value 0 = if 0 0 exit then
	value abs to absolute
	absolute log10 round-down 1+ to exponent
	absolute 10 exponent ^ / 1000000 * round to mantissa
	mantissa 1000000 >= if mantissa 10 / round to mantissa ++ exponent then
	mantissa 100000 < if mantissa 10 * to mantissa -- exponent then
	value 0 < mantissa exponent pack-float ;

\ print a float as F. does (0AB1-0B10): a minus sign; E format with the point after the first digit outside 1.0E-4 to 1.0E9; a point before leading zeros, the digits, the point where the exponent passes zero
: print-float ( low high -- )
	| low high |
	low high mantissa-digits to digits
	digits ( 0 > ) any? not if 48 print-char 46 print-char 32 print-char exit then
	high 8 rshift to exponent-byte
	exponent-byte 128 bit-and if 45 print-char then
	exponent-byte 127 bit-and to exponent-byte
	0 to original-exponent
	exponent-byte 1- to below
	below 0x49 >= below 0x3C < or if
		exponent-byte to original-exponent
		0x41 to exponent-byte
	then
	0x40 exponent-byte - to leading-zeros
	leading-zeros 0 >= if
		46 print-char
		0 leading-zeros 1 do k 48 print-char loop
	then
	begin
		digits ( 0 > ) any? exponent-byte 0x40 > or
	while
		digits 0 @i 48 + print-char
		digits 1 skip 0 add-last! to digits
		-- exponent-byte
		exponent-byte 0x40 = if 46 print-char then
	repeat
	original-exponent 0 = if 32 print-char exit then
	69 print-char
	original-exponent 0x41 - print-signed ;
